  "explanation": "The proposal introduces an integrated framework by adapting latent-space probing techniques—originally designed for novelty judgment tasks like Think-Probe-Respond—to steer multi-agent scientific ideation and iterative revision loops. While multi-agent ideation and latent probing for judgment exist independently in prior work, combining them to dynamically overcome medium-novelty biases during generation represents a novel and cohesive methodological extension.",
  "problems": [
    "The proposal relies on training a lightweight linear probe using a small supervised dataset of annotated hidden states within a constrained 6-week project window, which may be insufficient to guarantee robust generalization across diverse scientific domains.",
    "Adapting internal state probes—which are typically trained to classify static judgment outputs—to dynamically steer text generation loops introduces complex intervention dynamics that are underexplored."
  ],
  "improvements": [
    "Clarify the exact mechanism by which latent probe activations trigger structural contrastive prompts during token generation or revision steps.",
    "Provide a preliminary validation or pilot experiment demonstrating that linear probes trained on smaller open-weights models (like Llama-3-8B) can reliably detect novelty states during generative dialogue."
  ],
